{
  "name": "Infrastructure Cost Review",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Review changes for AWS infrastructure cost impact: Lambda sizing, S3 storage/transfer, API Gateway, data egress, and log retention",
  "when": {
    "type": "preToolUse",
    "toolTypes": ["write"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Before writing this file, review the change for AWS infrastructure cost concerns. Check for: (1) Lambda memory/timeout sizing — is it bounded and appropriate for a streaming workload, not oversized, (2) provisioned concurrency or always-on capacity that incurs standing cost, (3) S3 cost — storage class, lifecycle/expiration rules for test objects and versions, unnecessary retained data, (4) data transfer/egress cost from streaming large objects (e.g. the 15MB test file) out of S3 and API Gateway, (5) API Gateway request/data costs, (6) CloudWatch Logs retention set to a finite period (not infinite), (7) resources left running after tests (no cleanup), (8) estimated cost impact of the change. If any cost concerns are found, describe them. If the change has no infrastructure cost implications, confirm it is safe."
  }
}
